**What changed:** Angular 22.0 adds a new public API `injectAsync` in `@angular/core` (exported from `packages/core/src/di/inject_async.ts`, re-exported via `packages/core/src/di/index.ts`), alongside `InjectAsyncOptions`, `PrefetchTrigger`, and the `onIdle` helper — all marked `@publicApi 22.0` (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/444b024d49725afc8b40aec67cfdb63a1f7f23ea). API golden signature: `export function injectAsync<T>(loader: () => Promise<ProviderToken<T>>, options?: InjectAsyncOptions): () => Promise<T>;`. It must be called in an injection context (`assertInInjectionContext`), captures the current `Injector` via `inject(Injector)`, and returns a memoized function that lazily resolves the `import()` loader and calls `injector.get(type)`. The injected service must be auto-provided (`@Injectable({providedIn: 'root'})` or `@Service()`). Optional `options.prefetch` accepts a `PrefetchTrigger`; `onIdle(options?: {timeout?: number})` returns a `Promise<void>` that resolves when the browser is idle, e.g. `injectAsync(.., {prefetch: onIdle})` or `{prefetch: () => onIdle({timeout: 100})}` (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/angular/angular/444b024d49725afc8b40aec67cfdb63a1f7f23ea/packages/core/src/di/inject_async.ts).

**Affects:** Nothing existing — this is an additive new API; no existing code, config, or dependency changes are required to upgrade. Applications may adopt it to replace hand-rolled lazy-injection helpers (the Angular docs site deleted its own `inject-async.ts` helper and `mockAsyncProvider` in this commit, using plain `{provide: X, useClass: FakeX}` TestBed providers instead).

**Action:** none

**Before/after:**
