**What changed:** `resource()`'s `params` function (and `httpResource`'s url/request function) may now throw special values to force a status transition: `ResourceParamsStatus.IDLE` → resource becomes `idle` (equivalent to returning `undefined`), `ResourceParamsStatus.LOADING` → `loading`, and any `Error` object → `error`, reported via `.error()` (commit 2206efa). New public API in `@angular/core`: `class ResourceParamsStatus extends Error` with `static readonly IDLE` and `static readonly LOADING`; `interface ResourceParamsContext { readonly chain: <T>(resource: Resource<T>) => T }`; and `class ResourceDependencyError extends Error` with `readonly dependency: Resource<unknown>` (name `'ResourceDependencyError'`, `cause` set to the dependency's `error()`). `BaseResourceOptions.params` signature changed from `params?: () => R` to `params?: (ctx: ResourceParamsContext) => R`, and every `HttpResourceFn` overload (including `arrayBuffer`, `blob`, `text`) changed from `url: () => string | undefined` / `request: () => HttpResourceRequest | undefined` to `(ctx: ResourceParamsContext) => ...`. `ctx.chain(otherResource)` returns the other resource's value or propagates its idle/loading/error state forward (an errored dependency surfaces as `ResourceDependencyError`). (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/2206efa55fc1de160333d62680f8893c47525335)

**Affects:** Applications using `resource()` from `@angular/core` or `httpResource()` from `@angular/common/http` — new capability; existing `params: () => R` / `url: () => string` call sites still typecheck since the context parameter is optional to implement. Only affected if code previously threw plain values from `params` expecting an error status, or hardcoded chained-resource status checks.

**Action:** none (opt-in feature). Optionally re-verify that `params`/`request` functions that throw non-`Error` values still behave as expected, and consider adopting `({chain}) => ...` in place of manual `status()` checks when one resource depends on another.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// new public API added by the commit (goldens/public-api/core/index.api.md)
export interface ResourceParamsContext {
    readonly chain: <T>(resource: Resource<T>) => T;
}

export class ResourceParamsStatus extends Error {
    static readonly IDLE: ResourceParamsStatus;
    static readonly LOADING: ResourceParamsStatus;
}

// httpResource: url/request function now receives the context
httpResource(({chain}) => chain(endpoint), {injector: TestBed.inject(Injector)});
```

Note: `ResourceParamsStatus` is documented in the source as throwable from a resource's `params` **or `request`** function, so the capability is not limited to `params` (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/2206efa55fc1de160333d62680f8893c47525335). `@experimental` markers on the `httpResource` overloads are unchanged (still `19.2`). No breaking rename or removal accompanies this commit.

**What changed:** A new public method `getFixture<T = unknown>(): ComponentFixture<T>` was added to the `TestBed` interface and `TestBedImpl` class. This method retrieves the most recently created `ComponentFixture` instance. If multiple fixtures have been created, the method throws an error to prevent tests from depending on fixture creation order. If no fixture has been created, it also throws an error. Static and instance accessors are available: `TestBed.getFixture()` or `getTestBed().getFixture()`. This method is particularly useful for retrieving fixtures created in `beforeEach` hooks within `it` blocks.

**Affects:** Angular unit tests using `TestBed`.

**Action:** none

**Before/after:**
