**What changed:** `provideClientHydration` now enables incremental hydration by default; without any opt-out feature it adds `ɵwithIncrementalHydration()` internally. A new public feature `withNoIncrementalHydration(): HydrationFeature<HydrationFeatureKind.NoIncrementalHydration>` (tagged `@publicApi 22.0`) disables it; passing both `withIncrementalHydration()` and `withNoIncrementalHydration()` in one `provideClientHydration()` call throws a `RuntimeError` with `RuntimeErrorCode.HYDRATION_CONFLICTING_FEATURES` in `ngDevMode` ("Configuration error: found both withIncrementalHydration() and withNoIncrementalHydration()... which is a contradiction"). `HydrationFeatureKind` gains the member `NoIncrementalHydration` (value `5`) and `withNoIncrementalHydration` is re-exported from `@angular/platform-browser` (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/68628dd45bfcf4ea33bc00798bab1e4ab9da804c, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/angular/angular/68628dd45bfcf4ea33bc00798bab1e4ab9da804c/packages/platform-browser/src/hydration.ts).

**Affects:** Applications that call `provideClientHydration()` (with or without existing features like `withEventReplay()`, `withHttpTransferCacheOptions()`, etc.) and did not previously call `withIncrementalHydration()`.

**Action:** required: a schematic migration registered as `incremental-hydration` (version `22.0.0`, factory `./bundles/incremental-hydration.cjs#migrate`) automatically appends `withNoIncrementalHydration()` (imported from `@angular/platform-browser`) to every `provideClientHydration()` call that lacks `withIncrementalHydration()`, preserving pre-v22 behavior. Run `ng update` to apply it; or manually add `withNoIncrementalHydration()` where incremental hydration must stay off, or remove the opt-out to adopt incremental hydration. Re-verify hydration behavior on pages using `hydrate` triggers.

**Before/after:**
```ts
// Before (v21: incremental hydration OFF unless explicitly enabled)
import { provideClientHydration } from '@angular/platform-browser';
provideClientHydration();

// After (v22: incremental hydration ON by default)
import { provideClientHydration } from '@angular/platform-browser';
provideClientHydration(); // now implicitly includes ɵwithIncrementalHydration()

// Opt out (added by the incremental-hydration schematic)
import { provideClientHydration, withNoIncrementalHydration } from '@angular/platform-browser';
provideClientHydration(withNoIncrementalHydration());
```

**What changed:** `SharedStylesHost.removeHost(hostNode)` (in `packages/platform-browser/src/dom/shared_styles_host.ts`) previously only did `this.hosts.delete(hostNode)`, leaving `<style>` and `<link>` tags for that host in the DOM — a memory leak, worsened when the same host is added/removed repeatedly, since styles were "consistently reappended but never removed." Now `removeHost` iterates over `this.inline` and `this.external` records and calls `element.remove()` on any element whose `parentNode === hostNode`, keeping the rest in `record.elements` (d45b7a91f961ee40e3ea0f0ae837bf543bddb520). Marked `BREAKING CHANGE`: styles are removed when no longer used by an associated `host`, but "other DOM on the page may still be affected by those styles if not leveraging `ViewEncapsulation.Emulated` or if those styles are used by elements outside of Angular, potentially causing other DOM to appear unstyled." Tests confirm `ssh.addStyles(['a {}'])` / `ssh.addStyles([], ['component.css'])` output (`<style>a {}</style>`, `<link rel="stylesheet" href="component.css">`) is emptied from the host after `ssh.removeHost(someHost)`.

**Affects:** Applications using `SharedStylesHost` with multiple hosts (e.g. multiple apps/bootstrap on a page, or dynamic host add/remove) whose component styles are shared with or relied upon by non-Angular DOM, or that do not use `ViewEncapsulation.Emulated`.

**Action:** none (no code/config change required); re-verify that styling of non-Angular or cross-component DOM still renders correctly after hosts are removed, and that no elements unintentionally lose styles.

**Before/after:**
```typescript
// Before (21.2): removeHost only dropped the host reference
removeHost(hostNode: Node): void {
  this.hosts.delete(hostNode);
}

// After (22.0): also detaches that host's <style>/<link> elements
removeHost(hostNode: Node): void {
  this.hosts.delete(hostNode);

  for (const record of [...this.inline.values(), ...this.external.values()]) {
    const remaining: Array<HTMLStyleElement | HTMLLinkElement> = [];
    for (const element of record.elements) {
      if (element.parentNode === hostNode) {
        element.remove();
      } else {
        remaining.push(element);
      }
    }
    record.elements = remaining;
  }
}
```
(https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/d45b7a91f961ee40e3ea0f0ae837bf543bddb520)

