```

**What changed:** The `currentSnapshot` parameter (third argument) of `CanMatchFn` and the `canMatch` method of the `CanMatch` interface is now required (previously optional with a `?`). While the Router always provided this argument at runtime, it was only optional in the types to avoid a breaking change in a minor version. Existing class implementations of `CanMatch` or function implementations typed as `CanMatchFn` must now include the third argument `currentSnapshot: PartialMatchRouteSnapshot` to satisfy the interface and compile successfully. (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/67452, https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/579440170b372f8348cf3e5b5ce9f9f430093947, https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/579440170b372f8348cf3e5b5ce9f9f430093947.patch)

**Affects:** Applications with existing class implementations of `CanMatch` or function implementations typed as `CanMatchFn` that omit the third `currentSnapshot` parameter. (https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/67452)

**Action:** required: Update `CanMatchFn` function implementations and `CanMatch` interface `canMatch` methods to include the required third argument `currentSnapshot: PartialMatchRouteSnapshot`. An automated migration named `can-match-snapshot-required` is available in the `@angular/core` schematics to assist with this update. (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/8216d349768687ed0cf9ef6e1d737e7db9c9e28b)

